  "summary": "require-i18next preinstall hex-decodes and executes curl exfiltrating host identity and /etc/passwd",
  "details": "On npm install, the package's preinstall lifecycle script reads a hex-encoded command from preinstall.json, decodes it with Buffer.from(..., 'hex'), and executes the result via child_process.exec. The decoded command invokes curl to POST the output of whoami, pwd, hostname, and the contents of /etc/passwd to https://eobdzec83knbura.m.pipedream.net, an attacker-controlled Pipedream webhook. The hex encoding hides the network destination and command contents from casual inspection of the manifest. The package name resembles the popular i18next library, consistent with a typosquat lure.",
